# JetBrains
.idea

# Bazel convenience symlinks (bazel-42, bazel-bin, bazel-out, bazel-testlogs).
# They point into ~/.cache/bazel/...; the execroot they target symlinks .git
# back here, which makes editors detect a phantom second repository.
/bazel-*

# C build artifacts (e.g. from `make`/manual cc inside deliverable while testing)
*.o
*.a
*.out

# These executables are named by their subjects and have no extension, so none
# of the rules above cover them. Running `make` by hand in the deliverable
# leaves one where the next `git add -A` would commit a binary -- and
# //tools:submit would then push it to Vogsphere, since its own exclude list is
# extension-based too.
c-piscine-rush-02/deliverable/ex00/rush-02
c-piscine-bsq/deliverable/ex00/bsq

# Shell-piscine deliverables are generated from generators/ (bazel run //...:generate)
c-piscine-shell-*/deliverable/

# clangd's per-project preamble/index cache (created next to compile_flags.txt)
/.cache/


# Per-machine Bazel overrides (cache location etc). The correct value differs
# on every machine, so unlike .submit-level this one must not be shared.
.bazelrc.local

# Editor detritus. tools/header_art.txt is tracked on purpose; its .backup is not.
*.backup

# 42's own documents: the per-module subject PDFs and the Norm. They are 42's to
# hand out, not this project's to redistribute, so none are shipped here — you
# download your own from the intranet. Ignored so that dropping them into a
# module directory (which is a perfectly good place to keep them) cannot commit
# them into a fork by accident. Tracking one anyway: `git add -f <file>`.
*.pdf

# 42 issues this dictionary with rush-02's subject: yours to fetch,
# not this project's to redistribute. Matched at any depth, because the
# path is an argument to your program, so a copy is as likely to sit
# beside your sources as at the module root. The harness's own fixtures
# are named differently (ref.dict, quirks.dict, ...) and are unaffected.
numbers.dict
